<body><div class=WordSection1>
<p class=inst>Sardar Vallabhbhai National Institute of Technology (SVNIT), Surat</p>
<p class=dept>Department of Artificial Intelligence</p>
<p class=course>Agentic AI (IA462) &mdash; Semester VIII</p>
<hr>
<table class=g><tr><th>Name</th><th>Roll No.</th><th>Experiment</th><th>Date</th></tr><tr><td>&nbsp;</td><td>U23AI042</td><td>9</td><td>31 October 2026</td></tr></table>
<h1>Experiment 9</h1>
<h1 class=sub>Artificial Neural Network &mdash; Multilayer Perceptron Trained by Backpropagation</h1>
<h2>Aim</h2>
<p>To study the multilayer feed-forward neural network and implement the backpropagation algorithm to learn the XOR function, a non-linearly separable mapping that a single-layer perceptron cannot represent, and to analyse the effect of the number of hidden units, learning rate, weight initialisation and hidden activation function on network convergence.</p>
<h2>Theory</h2>
<p>A single-layer perceptron computes a single separating hyperplane <i>w</i><sub>1</sub><i>x</i><sub>1</sub> + <i>w</i><sub>2</sub><i>x</i><sub>2</sub> + <i>b</i> = 0 in the input space, so it can partition only linearly separable classes. The XOR (exclusive OR) function is fundamentally non-linearly separable: no single straight line can place patterns (0, 1) and (1, 0) on one side while keeping (0, 0) and (1, 1) on the other. A multilayer feed-forward neural network overcomes this limitation by introducing one or more hidden layers of non-linear processing units. The hidden neurons transform the input into an intermediate representation space where the four XOR patterns become linearly separable, allowing the output neuron to form a separating decision boundary.</p>
<p>The network is trained using the <b>Backpropagation</b> algorithm via gradient descent on the squared error:</p>
<ul><li><b>Forward Pass</b>: Compute activations layer by layer: <i>a</i><sub>1</sub> = &sigma;(<i>x</i> &middot; <i>W</i><sub>1</sub> + <i>b</i><sub>1</sub>), <i>a</i><sub>2</sub> = &sigma;(<i>a</i><sub>1</sub> &middot; <i>W</i><sub>2</sub> + <i>b</i><sub>2</sub>), where &sigma;(<i>z</i>) = 1 / (1 + <i>e</i><sup>&minus;<i>z</i></sup>) is the logistic sigmoid, with derivative &sigma;'(<i>z</i>) = <i>a</i>(1 &minus; <i>a</i>).</li><li><b>Objective Function</b>: Squared error <i>E</i> = &frac12; &sum; (<i>a</i><sub>2</sub> &minus; <i>y</i>)<sup>2</sup>, reported per epoch as the mean squared error (MSE) across the four patterns.</li><li><b>Deltas (Chain Rule)</b>: Output layer error delta &delta;<sub>2</sub> = (<i>a</i><sub>2</sub> &minus; <i>y</i>) &odot; <i>a</i><sub>2</sub>(1 &minus; <i>a</i><sub>2</sub>). Hidden layer error delta &delta;<sub>1</sub> = (&delta;<sub>2</sub> &middot; <i>W</i><sub>2</sub><sup><i>T</i></sup>) &odot; <i>a</i><sub>1</sub>(1 &minus; <i>a</i><sub>1</sub>). The error of each hidden unit is thus the output error weighted by that unit's contribution to it.</li><li><b>Parameter Updates</b>: <i>W</i><sub>2</sub> &larr; <i>W</i><sub>2</sub> &minus; &eta; &middot; <i>a</i><sub>1</sub><sup><i>T</i></sup> &delta;<sub>2</sub>, <i>W</i><sub>1</sub> &larr; <i>W</i><sub>1</sub> &minus; &eta; &middot; <i>x</i><sup><i>T</i></sup> &delta;<sub>1</sub>, with biases updated by the column sums of the respective deltas; &eta; is the learning rate.</li></ul>
<p class=cap>Table 1. The XOR Logic Truth Table and Training Targets.</p>
<table class=g><tr><th style='width:20%'>Pattern</th><th style='width:25%'>x<sub>1</sub></th><th style='width:25%'>x<sub>2</sub></th><th style='width:30%'>Target y (XOR)</th></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>0</td><td>0</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>0</td><td>1</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>3</td><td>1</td><td>0</td><td>1</td></tr><tr><td>4</td><td>1</td><td>1</td><td>0</td></tr></table>
<h2>Algorithm</h2>
<h3>Part A &mdash; Network Architecture &amp; Initialisation</h3>
<ol><li>Configure network architecture: <i>n</i> = 2 inputs, <i>h</i> hidden units, <i>m</i> = 1 output.</li><li>Set learning rate &eta;, maximum training epochs, and MSE convergence tolerance tol.</li><li>Initialise weights <i>W</i><sub>1</sub> and <i>W</i><sub>2</sub> randomly from Uniform[&minus;1, 1], and biases <i>b</i><sub>1</sub>, <i>b</i><sub>2</sub> to zero. Randomness breaks symmetry so hidden units differentiate and learn distinct features.</li></ol>
<h3>Part B &mdash; Backpropagation Training Loop</h3>
<ol><li><b>Forward Pass</b>: Compute hidden activations <i>a</i><sub>1</sub> and output <i>a</i><sub>2</sub> for all four training patterns. Compute epoch mean squared error MSE = &frac12; &times; mean((<i>a</i><sub>2</sub> &minus; <i>y</i>)<sup>2</sup>).</li><li><b>Backward Pass</b>: Compute output delta &delta;<sub>2</sub> = (<i>a</i><sub>2</sub> &minus; <i>y</i>) &odot; <i>a</i><sub>2</sub>(1 &minus; <i>a</i><sub>2</sub>) and hidden delta &delta;<sub>1</sub> = (&delta;<sub>2</sub> &middot; <i>W</i><sub>2</sub><sup><i>T</i></sup>) &odot; <i>f</i>'(<i>a</i><sub>1</sub>).</li><li><b>Gradient Updates</b>: Update weights and biases using learning rate &eta;.</li><li><b>Termination Check</b>: Stop when MSE &lt; tol and all four predictions round correctly (&round;(<i>a</i><sub>2</sub>) = <i>y</i>), or when maximum epochs is reached.</li></ol>
<h2>Source Code (exp9_mlp.py)</h2>
<pre class=code style='font-size:7.0pt'>&quot;&quot;&quot;SVNIT Surat — Department of Artificial Intelligence
Agentic AI (IA462) — Semester VIII
Experiment 9: Artificial Neural Network — Multilayer Perceptron Trained by Backpropagation
Roll No: U23AI042
&quot;&quot;&quot;

import os
import numpy as np

os.makedirs(&quot;outputs&quot;, exist_ok=True)

X = np.array([[0, 0], [0, 1], [1, 0], [1, 1]], dtype=np.float64)
Y = np.array([[0], [1], [1], [0]], dtype=np.float64)

def sigmoid(z):
    z = np.clip(z, -25.0, 25.0)
    return 1.0 / (1.0 + np.exp(-z))

def sigmoid_deriv(a):
    return a * (1.0 - a)

def tanh_act(z):
    return np.tanh(z)

def tanh_deriv(a):
    return 1.0 - a ** 2

class MLP:
    def __init__(self, n_input, n_hidden, n_output, lr=0.5, seed=42,
                 zero_init=False, hidden_activation=&quot;sigmoid&quot;):
        rng = np.random.RandomState(seed)
        if zero_init:
            self.W1 = np.zeros((n_input, n_hidden))
            self.b1 = np.zeros((1, n_hidden))
            self.W2 = np.zeros((n_hidden, n_output))
            self.b2 = np.zeros((1, n_output))
        else:
            self.W1 = rng.uniform(-1, 1, (n_input, n_hidden))
            self.b1 = np.zeros((1, n_hidden))
            self.W2 = rng.uniform(-1, 1, (n_hidden, n_output))
            self.b2 = np.zeros((1, n_output))
        self.lr = lr
        if hidden_activation == &quot;tanh&quot;:
            self.h_act = tanh_act
            self.h_deriv = tanh_deriv
        else:
            self.h_act = sigmoid
            self.h_deriv = sigmoid_deriv
    
    def forward(self, X):
        self.z1 = X @ self.W1 + self.b1
        self.a1 = self.h_act(self.z1)
        self.z2 = self.a1 @ self.W2 + self.b2
        self.a2 = sigmoid(self.z2)
        return self.a2
    
    def backward(self, X, Y):
        delta2 = (self.a2 - Y) * sigmoid_deriv(self.a2)
        delta1 = (delta2 @ self.W2.T) * self.h_deriv(self.a1)
        self.W2 -= self.lr * (self.a1.T @ delta2)
        self.b2 -= self.lr * np.sum(delta2, axis=0, keepdims=True)
        self.W1 -= self.lr * (X.T @ delta1)
        self.b1 -= self.lr * np.sum(delta1, axis=0, keepdims=True)
    
    def mse(self, Y):
        return 0.5 * np.mean((self.a2 - Y) ** 2)
    
    def train(self, X, Y, max_epochs=6000, tol=0.005, check_interval=1, record_history=False):
        history = []
        for epoch in range(1, max_epochs + 1):
            self.forward(X)
            if record_history:
                history.append(self.mse(Y))
            self.backward(X, Y)
            if epoch % check_interval == 0:
                err = self.mse(Y)
                preds = (self.a2 &gt; 0.5).astype(float)
                if err &lt; tol and np.all(preds == Y):
                    return epoch, err, history
        return max_epochs, self.mse(Y), history

if __name__ == &quot;__main__&quot;:
    # Reference Run
    net = MLP(n_input=2, n_hidden=2, n_output=1, lr=0.5, seed=42)
    epochs, final_mse, history = net.train(X, Y, max_epochs=6000, tol=0.005, record_history=True)
    outputs = net.forward(X)

    print(&quot;=&quot; * 60)
    print(&quot;REFERENCE RUN: 2-2-1 MLP, lr=0.5, seed=42&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 60)
    print(f&quot;Epochs to convergence: {epochs}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Final MSE:             {final_mse:.6f}&quot;)
    print(&quot;\nLearned Outputs:&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  (0,0) -&gt; {outputs[0,0]:.4f}  (target: 0)&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  (0,1) -&gt; {outputs[1,0]:.4f}  (target: 1)&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  (1,0) -&gt; {outputs[2,0]:.4f}  (target: 1)&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  (1,1) -&gt; {outputs[3,0]:.4f}  (target: 0)&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  Correct: {np.all((outputs &gt; 0.5).astype(float) == Y)}&quot;)
    print(&quot;\nLearned Weights:&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  W1 (2x2):\n{net.W1}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  b1 (1x2): {net.b1}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  W2 (2x1):\n{net.W2}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;  b2 (1x1): {net.b2}&quot;)

    # Exercise 1: Sweep
    hidden_units = [1, 2, 3, 4, 8]
    learning_rates = [0.1, 0.5, 1.0]
    n_seeds = 20
    MAX_EPOCHS = 5000
    TOL = 0.005

    print(&quot;\n&quot; + &quot;=&quot; * 85)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 1: HIDDEN UNIT &amp; LEARNING RATE SWEEP (20 seeds per setting)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 85)
    header = f&quot;{&#x27;h&#x27;:&gt;3}  {&#x27;lr&#x27;:&gt;5}  {&#x27;Converged&#x27;:&gt;10}  {&#x27;Conv. Rate&#x27;:&gt;10}  {&#x27;Median Epochs&#x27;:&gt;14}  {&#x27;Min&#x27;:&gt;6}  {&#x27;Max&#x27;:&gt;6}&quot;
    print(header)
    print(&quot;-&quot; * len(header))

    for h in hidden_units:
        for lr in learning_rates:
            conv_count = 0
            conv_epochs = []
            for seed in range(n_seeds):
                net_test = MLP(n_input=2, n_hidden=h, n_output=1, lr=lr, seed=seed)
                ep, mse_final, _ = net_test.train(X, Y, max_epochs=MAX_EPOCHS, tol=TOL, check_interval=10)
                if ep &lt; MAX_EPOCHS:
                    conv_count += 1
                    conv_epochs.append(ep)
            med_ep = int(np.median(conv_epochs)) if conv_epochs else -1
            min_ep = min(conv_epochs) if conv_epochs else -1
            max_ep = max(conv_epochs) if conv_epochs else -1
            rate_str = f&quot;{conv_count}/{n_seeds}&quot;
            med_str = f&quot;{med_ep}&quot; if med_ep &gt; 0 else &quot;N/A&quot;
            min_str = f&quot;{min_ep}&quot; if min_ep &gt; 0 else &quot;N/A&quot;
            max_str = f&quot;{max_ep}&quot; if max_ep &gt; 0 else &quot;N/A&quot;
            print(f&quot;{h:&gt;3}  {lr:&gt;5.1f}  {rate_str:&gt;10}  {conv_count/n_seeds:&gt;10.0%}  {med_str:&gt;14}  {min_str:&gt;6}  {max_str:&gt;6}&quot;)
        print()

    # Exercise 2A: Zero init
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 70)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 2A: ZERO WEIGHT INITIALISATION (2-2-1, lr=0.5)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 70)
    net_zero = MLP(n_input=2, n_hidden=2, n_output=1, lr=0.5, seed=42, zero_init=True)
    ep_zero, mse_zero, _ = net_zero.train(X, Y, max_epochs=5000, tol=0.005, record_history=False)
    out_zero = net_zero.forward(X)
    print(f&quot;Epochs used:  {ep_zero}  {&#x27;(CONVERGED)&#x27; if ep_zero &lt; 5000 else &#x27;(DID NOT CONVERGE)&#x27;}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Final MSE:    {mse_zero:.6f}&quot;)
    print(&quot;\nOutputs:&quot;)
    for i in range(4):
        print(f&quot;  ({int(X[i,0])},{int(X[i,1])}) -&gt; {out_zero[i,0]:.4f}  (target: {int(Y[i,0])})&quot;)
    print(f&quot;\nHidden Weight Matrix W1 after training:\n{net_zero.W1}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;\nHidden Bias b1 after training:\n{net_zero.b1}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;\nOutput Weight Matrix W2 after training:\n{net_zero.W2}&quot;)

    # Exercise 2B: Tanh activation
    print(&quot;\n&quot; + &quot;=&quot; * 70)
    print(&quot;EXERCISE 2B: TANH HIDDEN ACTIVATION (2-2-1, lr=0.5, seed=42)&quot;)
    print(&quot;=&quot; * 70)
    net_tanh = MLP(n_input=2, n_hidden=2, n_output=1, lr=0.5, seed=42, hidden_activation=&quot;tanh&quot;)
    ep_tanh, mse_tanh, _ = net_tanh.train(X, Y, max_epochs=5000, tol=0.005, record_history=False)
    out_tanh = net_tanh.forward(X)
    print(f&quot;Epochs to convergence: {ep_tanh}  {&#x27;(CONVERGED)&#x27; if ep_tanh &lt; 5000 else &#x27;(DID NOT CONVERGE)&#x27;}&quot;)
    print(f&quot;Final MSE:             {mse_tanh:.6f}&quot;)
    print(&quot;\nOutputs:&quot;)
    for i in range(4):
        print(f&quot;  ({int(X[i,0])},{int(X[i,1])}) -&gt; {out_tanh[i,0]:.4f}  (target: {int(Y[i,0])})&quot;)</pre>
